{"file":"crowdstrike-falcon-fusion-1.2.0-v2.zip","bytes":670491,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"crowdstrike-falcon-fusion","description":"CrowdStrike Falcon Fusion skills for authoring, deploying, and executing Fusion workflows. Includes live action discovery, YAML authoring with schema validation, workflow import and release, execution monitoring, and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM lookup files.","version":"1.2.0","license":"MIT","keywords":["crowdstrike","falcon","fusion","soar","workflow","automation","security"]},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"crowdstrike-falcon-fusion","description":"CrowdStrike Falcon Fusion skills for authoring, deploying, and executing Fusion workflows. Includes live action discovery, YAML authoring with schema validation, workflow import and release, execution monitoring, and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM lookup files.","version":"1.2.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/CrowdStrike/fusion-skills","homepage":"https://github.com/CrowdStrike/fusion-skills","keywords":["crowdstrike","falcon","fusion","soar","workflow","automation","security"]},{"path":"plugin.json","name":"crowdstrike-falcon-fusion","description":"CrowdStrike Falcon Fusion skills for authoring, deploying, and executing Fusion workflows. Includes live action discovery, YAML authoring with schema validation, workflow import and release, execution monitoring, and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM lookup files.","version":"1.2.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/CrowdStrike/fusion-skills","homepage":"https://github.com/CrowdStrike/fusion-skills","keywords":["crowdstrike","falcon","fusion","soar","workflow","automation","security"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/authoring/SKILL.md","name":"authoring","description":"Discover Falcon Fusion actions via live API, author workflow YAML with correct schema, validate against Charlotte JSON schema, and use templates/examples. TRIGGER when user asks to write workflow YAML, find actions, validate a workflow, use CEL expressions, or needs action discovery. DO NOT TRIGGER for deploying, importing, executing, or monitoring workflows — use deployment or execution skills. DO NOT TRIGGER when the request is for a Falcon Foundry app, a UI extension/page, an API integration, custom actions from a third-party API, or a manifest.yml — those are foundry-skills territory; advise foundry-skills instead of authoring a workflow.","headings":["Falcon Fusion Workflow Authoring","Prerequisites","Core Workflow","1. Resolve action IDs (MANDATORY)","Search by name across all vendors (note the --search flag; a bare term errors)","Search within a specific vendor","Full schema for one action (input fields, class, plugin info)","2. Choose a trigger type","3. Author the YAML from a template","4. Add CEL expressions","5. Validate","Pre-flight + structural + API dry-run","Pre-flight + structural only (no API call)","Script Reference","Common Pitfalls / Counter-Rationalizations","Reading Guide","HTTP Actions (`Inline.HTTPRequest`)","Inline actions (`Inline.Python`, `Inline.QueryEvent`)"],"name_hint":"authoring"},{"path":"skills/deployment/SKILL.md","name":"deployment","description":"Import, release, and manage Falcon Fusion workflow definitions in a CID. TRIGGER when user asks to import a workflow, release a workflow version, list existing workflows, check for duplicates, or manage workflow definitions. DO NOT TRIGGER for writing YAML (use authoring), executing workflows, or monitoring (use execution).","headings":["Falcon Fusion Workflow Deployment","Prerequisites","Core Workflow","1. Validate the YAML first","2. Check for an existing workflow with the same name","Exact-name check (exit 0 if it exists, 1 if not)","Or extract the name straight from the YAML and check","3. Import the definition","Single file — validates and checks duplicates by default","A whole directory of definitions (all *.yaml/*.yml)","4. Release (enable) the workflow","1. Fix the condition in the SOURCE YAML (add cel_expression + else:).","Keep the workflow `name:` IDENTICAL — do NOT bump it to `<name>-v2`.","The name is the workflow's identity; --replace matches on it.","2. Re-validate — this now catches the release-failing shape pre-deploy:","3. Re-import with --replace: deletes the broken same-name definition and","imports the fixed YAML in one step (supported delete + import, not a patch).","Script Reference"],"name_hint":"deployment"},{"path":"skills/execution/SKILL.md","name":"execution","description":"Trigger Falcon Fusion workflows, monitor execution status, and debug failures. TRIGGER when user asks to run a workflow, check execution status, tail logs, get execution results, or debug a workflow failure. DO NOT TRIGGER for writing YAML (use authoring) or importing/releasing workflows (use deployment).","headings":["Falcon Fusion Workflow Execution","Prerequisites","Core Workflow","1. Verify the workflow is deployed and released","2. Trigger the workflow with a payload","Pass parameters inline as JSON","Or let the script prompt you interactively from the workflow's parameter schema","3. Monitor the execution","Tune the cadence for long-running workflows","4. Get the results","5. Debug failures","Script Reference","trigger_workflow.py","monitor_execution.py","get_execution_results.py","Common Pitfalls","Handoff"],"name_hint":"execution"},{"path":"skills/foundry-redirect/SKILL.md","name":"foundry-redirect","description":"TRIGGER when the user asks to \"build a Foundry app\", \"create a Foundry app\", mentions manifest.yml, or needs a UI page/extension, serverless function, collection, or a custom API integration from a third-party API (Okta, ServiceNow, Jira, etc.) built. DO NOT TRIGGER for a standalone Fusion workflow that only wires together existing actions. This skill declines Foundry-app requests and points to the crowdstrike-falcon-foundry plugin, so the redirect works even without Claude Code hooks; it yields to the real Foundry plugin when that plugin is also installed.","headings":["Falcon Foundry Redirect","What to do","When both plugins are installed","Foundry app vs. standalone workflow"],"name_hint":"foundry · redirect"},{"path":"skills/lookup-files/SKILL.md","name":"lookup-files","description":"Manage Falcon Next-Gen SIEM lookup files (CSV/JSON/TXT) for CQL match() queries. TRIGGER when user asks to create, list, update, or delete lookup files, or needs help with CQL match() function. DO NOT TRIGGER for Fusion workflows, action discovery, or workflow deployment — use the workflows/authoring/deployment skills.","headings":["Falcon Next-Gen SIEM Lookup Files","Prerequisites","Required API Scopes","Credentials","Core Workflow","Step 1 — List (check for duplicates)","Step 2 — Prepare the file","Step 3 — Upload","Step 4 — Verify","Step 5 — Use in CQL","Step 6 — Update","Step 7 — Delete","Lookup Files from Workflows","Script Reference","Common Pitfalls","Reading Guide"],"name_hint":"lookup · 文件"},{"path":"skills/setup/SKILL.md","name":"setup","description":"Configure CrowdStrike Falcon API credentials for the fusion-skills plugin. TRIGGER when user asks to set up credentials, configure API access, or runs into authentication errors.","headings":["Falcon Fusion Credential Setup","Step 1 — Check for existing credentials","Step 2 — Create the credentials file and have the user fill it in","CrowdStrike Falcon API credentials for fusion-skills.","Fill in client_id and client_secret below, then save this file.","# Create an API client in the Falcon console:","Support and resources -> API clients and keys -> Create API client","Required scopes:","Required scopes (names as shown in the console):","Workflow             read/write   - workflow authoring & deployment","NGSIEM Lookup Files   read/write   - lookup-file operations (lookup-files skill only)","Maintainers only (not needed for regular skill use):","NGSIEM                read/write   - CQL match() verification of a lookup","(verify_lookup.py / verify-workflows.sh --lookup-dir)","Add more clouds as needed (change `default` above to switch):","[us-1]","client_id = \"\"","client_secret = [已隐藏]"],"name_hint":"设置"},{"path":"skills/workflows/SKILL.md","name":"workflows","description":"Orchestrates the full Falcon Fusion workflow lifecycle from discovery through deployment and execution. TRIGGER when user asks to \"create a Fusion workflow\", \"build a Fusion playbook\", \"automate CrowdStrike actions\", or mentions Fusion workflows without specifying a sub-task. DO NOT TRIGGER when user is working in a Foundry app context, mentions manifest.yml, or asks to \"build a Foundry app\" — use foundry-skills instead.","headings":["Falcon Fusion Workflow Orchestrator","Decision Tree","Full Lifecycle Coordination","Delegation Examples","Cross-Plugin Advisory","Foundry app lifecycle (UI, functions, collections, manifest)","Use-Case Pattern Matching","Trigger Selection (route correctly)","Counter-Rationalizations","Reading Guide","Improving These Skills"],"name_hint":"流程"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Falcon Fusion Skills","Getting Started","Prerequisites","Install","Credentials","export FALCON_BASE_URL=https://api.crowdstrike.com  # US-1 (default)","US-2: https://api.us-2.crowdstrike.com · US-3: https://api.us-3.crowdstrike.com · EU-1: https://api.eu-1.crowdstrike.com · US-GOV-1: https://api.laggar.gcw.crowdstrike.com","Other Tools","Usage","Example prompt","How skill routing works","Skills","Architecture","Quick Start","Use Cases","Recommended Companion: Superpowers","Troubleshooting","Skills not invoked","Authentication failures","Stale action cache","Workflow won't execute","Testing","Unit tests (Python)","Fast checks (no API calls)","Skill test (single run)","Verify workflows","Multi-assistant smoke test","A/B test (baseline vs local branch)"]},{"path":"use-cases/README.md","headings":["Use Cases","How the Orchestrator Uses These","Available Use Cases","File Format","When to Use","Pattern","Key Actions","Gotchas","Ad